3	 * highlight in the review editor.
4	 *
5	 * The editor authors annotations with an eager "Pattern A" flow: clicking a
6	 * selection-toolbar button colorizes the selected text immediately, before the
7	 * composer collects a body. These steps verify that highlight is rendered
8	 * after the button click and removed after the composer is cancelled. Each
9	 * annotation leaf carries a per-kind `data-testid` (`annotation-<kind>`), the
10	 * stable selector the suite mandates over class/role selectors.
11	 *
12	 * @example
13	 *   Then the "comment" highlight is visible in the editor
14	 *   Then the "insertion" highlight is absent from the editor
15	 */
